{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789231199,"nonce":"vMPqiPuBSWG8Q9pI4NINim19rQI=","title":"Two string concatenations in one expression crash","message":"def h(digits: String): String { return \"a\" + \"b\" + digits }\n\ncrashes with SIGBUS; `\"a\" + digits` alone is fine. The inner `+` is a\ntyped-AST Binary the parser leaves typed Unknown, so when the outer `+`\nasks whether its left operand is a String (`resolve_actual_type` only\nlooks through variables) it is told Unknown, takes the integer path,\nand adds two pointers.\n\nFix: `resolve_expr_type` answers String for an Add whose operand is a\nString, and the concat check consults both operands' resolved types.","files":null}]}